1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
SOMETHING IS WRONG.
A dark LED. One wrong connection.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:20,000
SEE WHAT’S WRONG WITH YOUR CIRCUIT.
CircuitLens turns connections into explanations.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Choose a circuit. Trace the problem.
Seven generated fixtures. The real deterministic rule engine.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
One workbench. Three connected views.
Circuit image → editable topology → component properties.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Every connection is inspectable.
Select D1 in the topology to inspect its anode and cathode.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
From wires to reasoning.
The opening schematic illustrates the model behind the checks.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
REVERSED LED POLARITY
Observed: cathode toward power. Anode toward ground.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Why the LED stays dark.
Reverse bias prevents normal illumination.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
A specific, inspectable fix.
Disconnect power. Swap the LED leads. Confirm the model again.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:37,000
A person reviews every observation.
Accept, reject, or correct each proposed component and terminal.

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Uncertainty cannot become a fact silently.
Unknown accepted terminals block conversion. Live extraction remains unverified.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Correct. Confirm. Recheck.
D1: A = D12, B = D18. Editing clears the old result.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The connections check out.
9.1 mA is a simple series estimate, not a physical measurement.

14
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:20,000
VISUAL OBSERVATION → STRUCTURED CIRCUIT
Visual proposals pass through human review before becoming a netlist.

15
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:30,000
ENGINEERING RULES → DIAGNOSIS
Evidence, explanation, and a fix you can trace to a connection.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
AI OBSERVES. ENGINEERING RULES REASON.
CircuitLens. See the fault. Understand the fix.
